abstract: |
  AortaCFD is an open-source, automated pipeline for patient-specific aortic blood flow
  simulation. It streamlines the entire computational fluid dynamics (CFD) workflow from
  geometry preparation to post-processing, making advanced hemodynamic analysis accessible
  and reproducible. The software features two-stage physics-aware mesh optimization,
  automated three-element Windkessel boundary conditions with Murray's Law flow distribution,
  and comprehensive hemodynamic analysis tools. Built on OpenFOAM 12, AortaCFD reduces
  simulation setup time from hours to minutes while maintaining high accuracy validated
  against literature data. The modular Python architecture enables easy customization and
  extension for research applications.
